can-utils is the SocketCAN userspace toolset (candump, cansend, cangen,
canplayer, canbusload, canfdtest, asc2log, log2asc, canerrsim).

This is a FreeBSD port of github.com/linux-can/can-utils, adapted to build and
run against this project's in-kernel netcan (PF_CAN / AF_CAN, CAN_RAW + vcan)
stack. The Linux<->BSD differences are bridged by a small compat/ shim
(sockaddr_can BSD layout, <linux/*> header shims, SIOCGIFNAME -> if_indextoname,
Linux-only socket options stubbed). Only the RAW-CAN tools are built; the ISOTP,
J1939, BCM, gateway and slcan-line-discipline tools need kernel features not
present on FreeBSD and are omitted.
